---
import Layout from '../../frontend/layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../frontend/components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../frontend/components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Vitamin D & B12 Deficiency Test Report Explained | HealthSaral"
  description="India has the world's highest rates of Vitamin D and B12 deficiency. Learn what your Vitamin D and B12 blood test results mean, what causes deficiency, and how to correct it naturally."
>
  <Header />

  <main class="flex-grow">
    <section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-mesh-gradient pt-14 pb-16 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 border-b border-hairline">
      <div class="w-full max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-2 mb-6">
          <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-primary bg-primary/5 border border-primary/10 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full uppercase tracking-wide">Vitamin D</span>
          <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-primary bg-primary/5 border border-primary/10 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full uppercase tracking-wide">B12</span>
          <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-primary bg-primary/5 border border-primary/10 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full uppercase tracking-wide">Nutrition</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-display font-bold text-primary tracking-tight mb-4 text-balance">
          Vitamin D and B12 Deficiency: Reading Your Nutritional Blood Report
        </h1>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-muted max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
          Over 70% of Indians are Vitamin D deficient and B12 deficiency is rampant among vegetarians. If your report shows low values, here is exactly what it means and what to do.
        </p>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-4 mt-6 text-xs text-muted font-mono">
          <span>📅 Nov 3, 2026</span><span>•</span><span>⏱ 7 min read</span><span>•</span><span>✅ Doctor-Reviewed</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <article class="py-16 bg-canvas px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto prose dark:prose-invert prose-sm sm:prose-base font-sans text-ink leading-relaxed">

        <div class="bg-amber-50/50 dark:bg-amber-950/20 border border-amber-200/50 dark:border-amber-900/30 rounded-lg p-4 mb-8 text-sm text-amber-800 dark:text-amber-200">
          <strong>Medical Disclaimer:</strong> Do not start supplements based on this article alone. Supplement doses must be prescribed by a doctor based on your specific levels and health status.
        </div>

        <h2>Vitamin D (25-OH Vitamin D / Calciferol)</h2>
        <p>Vitamin D is a fat-soluble vitamin and hormone that your skin synthesizes when exposed to sunlight. Despite being a "sunny country," India has paradoxically high rates of Vitamin D deficiency — primarily because of indoor lifestyles, skin pigmentation (which filters UV), and dietary patterns.</p>

        <div class="bg-canvas-soft border border-hairline rounded-lg p-4 my-4">
          <p class="font-semibold text-primary mb-2">Vitamin D Normal Range (25-OH Vitamin D):</p>
          <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="text-sm w-full">
              <thead><tr class="border-b border-hairline"><th class="text-left p-2 text-primary">Level</th><th class="text-left p-2 text-primary">Status</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody class="divide-y divide-hairline/50">
                <tr><td class="p-2">&lt; 10 ng/mL</td><td class="p-2 text-red-600 font-semibold">Severe Deficiency</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-2">10 – 20 ng/mL</td><td class="p-2 text-orange-600 font-semibold">Deficiency</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-2">20 – 30 ng/mL</td><td class="p-2 text-amber-600 font-semibold">Insufficiency</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-2">30 – 100 ng/mL</td><td class="p-2 text-green-600 font-semibold">Optimal / Sufficient</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-2">&gt; 100 ng/mL</td><td class="p-2 text-red-600 font-semibold">Toxicity Risk</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3>Symptoms of Vitamin D Deficiency</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Bone and muscle pain (especially lower back and legs)</li>
          <li>Fatigue and low energy that doesn't improve with rest</li>
          <li>Frequent respiratory infections (colds, flu)</li>
          <li>Low mood or depression</li>
          <li>Hair loss</li>
          <li>In children: Rickets (soft bones, bowed legs)</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Vitamin D — Indian Food Sources</h3>
        <p>Very few Indian foods are naturally rich in Vitamin D (it is rare in plant foods). Best dietary sources include:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>🐟 <strong>Fatty fish:</strong> Rohu, catla, pomfret (highest sources)</li>
          <li>🥚 <strong>Egg yolk:</strong> Contains small but useful amounts</li>
          <li>🥛 <strong>Fortified milk and dairy:</strong> Some brands fortify milk with Vitamin D — check labels</li>
          <li>🍄 <strong>Mushrooms (sun-dried):</strong> UV-exposed mushrooms produce Vitamin D2</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Sunlight is the main source:</strong> 15–30 minutes of midday sun on arms and legs (without sunscreen) 3–4 times per week is recommended — though this varies with skin tone and season.</p>
        <p><strong>Supplementation:</strong> Most people with deficiency need oral supplements (Cholecalciferol D3). Doses are prescribed by a doctor based on level — common regimens include 60,000 IU weekly for 8–12 weeks, then a maintenance dose.</p>

        <h2>Vitamin B12 (Cobalamin)</h2>
        <p>Vitamin B12 is essential for red blood cell formation, DNA synthesis, and neurological function. It is found almost exclusively in animal products, making deficiency extremely common among vegetarians and vegans in India.</p>

        <div class="bg-canvas-soft border border-hairline rounded-lg p-4 my-4">
          <p class="font-semibold text-primary mb-2">Vitamin B12 Normal Range:</p>
          <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="text-sm w-full">
              <thead><tr class="border-b border-hairline"><th class="text-left p-2 text-primary">Level</th><th class="text-left p-2 text-primary">Status</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody class="divide-y divide-hairline/50">
                <tr><td class="p-2">&lt; 150 pg/mL</td><td class="p-2 text-red-600 font-semibold">Deficiency (Clinical)</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-2">150 – 200 pg/mL</td><td class="p-2 text-amber-600 font-semibold">Borderline / Low</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-2">200 – 900 pg/mL</td><td class="p-2 text-green-600 font-semibold">Normal</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-2">&gt; 900 pg/mL</td><td class="p-2 text-blue-600 font-semibold">High (supplement effect)</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3>Symptoms of B12 Deficiency</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Fatigue and weakness (anemia)</li>
          <li>Numbness or tingling in hands and feet (neuropathy)</li>
          <li>Memory problems, brain fog, difficulty concentrating</li>
          <li>Sore or inflamed tongue (glossitis)</li>
          <li>Mood changes: depression, irritability</li>
          <li>Pale or slightly yellow skin</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Warning:</strong> B12 deficiency neuropathy (nerve damage) can be irreversible if not treated promptly. Don't delay if you have neurological symptoms.</p>

        <h3>B12 — Indian Food Sources</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>🐟 <strong>Seafood and fish</strong> (highest sources — rohu, prawns, crab)</li>
          <li>🥚 <strong>Eggs</strong> — especially the yolk</li>
          <li>🥛 <strong>Dairy</strong> — dahi (curd), paneer, milk are good vegetarian sources</li>
          <li>🌱 <strong>Fortified foods</strong> — some nutritional yeast and plant-based milks are B12-fortified</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Vegetarians and Vegans:</strong> Dairy is your primary source, but many vegetarians still become deficient due to malabsorption. Supplementation with cyanocobalamin or methylcobalamin tablets is often the most reliable approach.</p>

        <h2>Iron and Ferritin — The Third Common Deficiency</h2>
        <p>Your nutritional panel may also include Serum Ferritin (iron stores) and Serum Iron. India has very high rates of iron deficiency, particularly among women of reproductive age.</p>
        <div class="bg-canvas-soft border border-hairline rounded-lg p-4 my-4">
          <ul class="text-sm space-y-1 m-0">
            <li><strong>Serum Ferritin (Women):</strong> 12 – 150 ng/mL | (Men) 12 – 300 ng/mL</li>
            <li><strong>Low Ferritin (&lt; 12):</strong> Iron store depletion — anemia risk even before Hb falls</li>
            <li><strong>Serum Iron:</strong> 60 – 170 µg/dL (normal)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-primary/20 bg-primary/5 rounded-lg p-6 my-8 text-center">
          <p class="text-primary font-display font-semibold text-lg mb-2">Get your nutritional report explained instantly</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted mb-4">Upload your Vitamin D, B12, iron report and get a free, personalized explanation with actionable Indian diet and supplement guidance.</p>
          <a href="/#upload-section" class="inline-block px-6 py-3 bg-accent hover:bg-accent/90 text-white font-sans font-medium text-sm rounded-full shadow-sm transition-all">
            Analyze My Nutrition Report Free →
          </a>
        </div>

      </div>
    </article>

    <section class="py-12 bg-canvas-soft border-t border-hairline px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-display font-bold text-primary mb-6">Related Patient Guides</h2>
        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
          <a href="/blog/understand-thyroid-test-report/" class="border border-hairline bg-canvas rounded-lg p-4 hover:border-primary/20 hover:shadow-sm transition-all">
            <span class="text-2xl block mb-2">🦋</span>
            <h3 class="text-sm font-display font-semibold text-primary mb-1">Understanding Thyroid Test Results: TSH, T3, T4</h3>
            <span class="text-xs text-muted">7 min read</span>
          </a>
          <a href="/blog/how-to-read-blood-test-report/" class="border border-hairline bg-canvas rounded-lg p-4 hover:border-primary/20 hover:shadow-sm transition-all">
            <span class="text-2xl block mb-2">🩸</span>
            <h3 class="text-sm font-display font-semibold text-primary mb-1">How to Read a Blood Test Report: Complete Guide</h3>
            <span class="text-xs text-muted">8 min read</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

